            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 5 changed paths in full. The change exports Binding.Check (renamed from check) in engine/reviewresult/rules.go and adds it as the first step of CheckExemption in engine/review/exempt.go.",
              "This tightens input handling: a stored exemption whose base is not a full git object name (e.g. an option-shaped value) is now refused before it can reach git. That reduces risk rather than adding it, and the validation is enforced in the backend function itself.",
              "Exporting Check adds no new data exposure or authorization surface; it is a pure validator that returns an error wrapping ErrInvalidBinding and takes no external input beyond the binding it is called on.",
              "Parse in engine/reviewresult/reviewresult.go only switches to the exported name, so its behavior is unchanged.",
              "The new tests in engine/review/exempt_check_test.go and engine/reviewresult/binding_check_test.go cover option-shaped bases, refs, abbreviations, bad digests and duplicate paths. They add no secrets or dependencies, so there is no scanner or dependency evidence to report.",
              "The added ordering check in CheckExemption could newly reject stored exemptions with an invalid binding. Those are the inputs the change is meant to refuse, and nothing here shows a valid baseline exemption being rejected, so there is no regression."
            ]
          }
        }
